# Change a claim's status: open (DRAFT -> OPEN), settle (OPEN -> SETTLED), approve (PENDING -> SETTLED),
# reject (PENDING -> OPEN, with the body's reason), void (DRAFT, OPEN or PENDING -> VOID),
# delete (DRAFT -> DELETED) or restore (DELETED -> DRAFT, only on the sheet's today it was deleted).
# A steward also voids a SETTLED claim within 7 days of its settlement (the status log's SETTLED date).
# A change its status does not allow is refused (400) and writes nothing.
# A claim dated inside a closed period is refused (400).
# A clerk settling a claim whose due is above the sheet's clerk limit makes it PENDING; a steward settles anything.
# Only a steward approves or rejects; the user who opened the claim cannot approve it.
# Only a steward re-settles (resettle: SETTLED -> SETTLED), freezing the claim again at today's figure as an open, unbound claim.
# While the sheet's void reasons list is not empty, a void needs the body's reason chosen from it (400 otherwise).
# A settle (or re-settle) with the body's batch token is part of a bulk settle: the claim takes that bulk settle's
# batch number (the sheet's next the first time), SETTLED or PENDING; a settle taken one at a time has none, and a
# re-settle taken one at a time keeps the batch the claim has.
# A claim that ends SETTLED (settled, approved or re-settled) notifies each user watching its person.
